                "tag": "div",
                "attrs": { "class": "grid two" },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "tag": "article",
                    "attrs": { "class": "card reveal" },
                    "children": [
                      { "tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["On your iPhone first"] },
                      {
                        "tag": "p",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          "Without sync — with no account or a free one — your records stay on the phone and in your own encrypted backups; only what you send yourself goes out: to the AI with your permission, an export, a debt or split-bill link. With an account and Premium they sync through Dibsly’s server, so your iPhones and my.dibslyapp.com show the same."
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "tag": "article",
                    "attrs": { "class": "card reveal" },
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "tag": "h3",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": ["The AI only with your permission"]
                      },
                      {
                        "tag": "p",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          "The AI is OpenAI, reached through Dibsly’s own server. Only what a feature needs is sent (another bank’s statement goes as the whole file, header included); OpenAI keeps it for at most 30 days and doesn’t train models on it."
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "tag": "p",
                        "attrs": { "class": "muted" },
                        "children": [
                          "Rates come from the National Bank of Ukraine, quotes from Nasdaq and Yahoo Finance; these requests carry none of your records. All the details are in the ",
